From 41e930bb742ed4569c13a0f9e9eb3a56b41b3144 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 26 Jul 2026 18:23:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(verification): official platform verification via
 @verifybot and the admin panel

Implements the official verified badge end to end: applications are filed through
a built-in system bot, decided in the admin panel, and the decision reaches
official clients as the standard checkmark.

Scope of the badge. This is the platform flag official clients render from
user#b1b8cc83 verified:flags.17 and channel#d49f34c6 verified:flags.7 (layer
228). It is deliberately not the third-party mechanism built on
botVerification#f93cd45c / bots.setCustomVerification#8b89dfbd /
bot_verification_icon, which stays untouched and is never conflated with it.

@verifybot. Reserved id 1250000011 and the reserved handle are seeded by
migration 0152, not created lazily, so the username is occupied from the moment
the schema is current. The dialog runs on the existing internal bot runtime
(BotResponder plus domain.BotChatState), so its messages are ordinary private
history: real message ids, dates and pts, present in dialogs, recoverable through
updates.getDifference. Inline keyboards work for internal bots for the first
time: messages.getBotCallbackAnswer previously always pushed to a bot session and
waited, which an in-process bot can never answer, so a synchronous branch now
serves them. Callback data carries only an opaque per-render token resolved
against the clicking user's own dialog state, so a click cannot name a peer at
all.

Applications. verification_applications is the durable audit subject with a
partial unique index for one live application per target, an append-only event
history, and a notification outbox. Approval is one transaction: status,
reviewer, history, outbox row and the peer flag commit together through a
callback that writes on the decision's own transaction, so "approved but not
verified" cannot exist. Every rule is re-checked at approval time against a fresh
snapshot, and optimistic locking on the application version makes two reviewers
deciding at once produce exactly one decision and one notification.

Admin panel. New Verification section with the queue, status counters, filters,
search, the review page with provenance and the applicant's current rights, and
claim / approve / reject / revoke actions behind the existing dry-run and command
journal. Two things the panel lacked and this feature requires: a permission
model (verification.review, verification.revoke; the master token stays
unrestricted so existing deployments are unaffected) and CSRF protection for the
cookie panel via a double-submit token.

Also fixes chatInvite#5c9d3702: verified, scam and fake (flags 7/8/9) were never
serialised, so an invite preview showed no badge until after joining.
